    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        -358.9923959032341,
        553.3187800066305
      ],
      "size": [
        290.1922351462714,
        97.95592567265356
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 1,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "SeedVR2 video upscale - ConvRot W4A8 build\n\nDiT: seedvr2_7b_convrot_w4a8.safetensors (4.44 GB on disk, ~5.7 GiB peak VRAM) from\nussoewwin/SeedVR2-ConvRot-INT8-and-w4a8 -> ComfyUI/models/SEEDVR2/\nVAE: ema_vae_fp16.safetensors from numz/SeedVR2_comfyUI -> same folder.\n\nThis is the legacy/standard DiT loader, the only node where W4A8 operation is officially\nguaranteed by the fork's README. Do not use the DisTorch2 loader with this checkpoint.\n\nSettings baked in: resolution 832 = shortest edge, so a 416x576 clip goes to 832x1152 -\nthe same geometry as the ComfyUI-Tessera refine, which makes the two directly comparable.\nbatch_size 33 obeys the 4n+1 rule (1, 5, 9, ... 33); uniform_batch_size pads the tail batch.\ncolor_correction lab tracks the source colour most faithfully. enable_debug is ON so the\nfirst run prints per-phase VRAM and timings.\n\nDials, in the order they matter:\n- blocks_to_swap on the DiT loader: 0 fits comfortably here; raise toward 36 only if VRAM\n  is tight. offload_device must be set (not \"none\") for swapping to do anything.\n- attention_mode: sdpa is the safe default. sageattn_2 / sageattn_3 are faster if the\n  packages are installed (sageattn_3 targets Blackwell, i.e. the 5090).\n- input_noise_scale 0.1-0.3, then latent_noise_scale 0.05-0.15: ByteDance's own note says\n  SeedVR2 over-generates detail on lightly degraded input - 480p/720p AIGC clips included.\n  If the output looks waxy or over-crisp, these two dials are the fix, not the model.\n- VAE device can be a second GPU (cuda:2) to keep the DiT card clear; encode_tiled /\n  decode_tiled are already on.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
